PN,41207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F412A1786915122
OL,3,CSinn Fein condemn burning of images of
OL,4,CFirst Minister on bonfire
OL,6,FReferring to the images of Sinn Fein
OL,7,Fvice president Ms O'Neill being burnt
OL,8,Fon a bonfire, Mr Finucane said: "These
OL,9,Fbonfires are not republican. They are
OL,10,Fanti-people, anti-community, anti-
OL,11,Fdemocratic and are, in their hate-
OL,12,Ffilled sectarianism, the very
OL,13,Fantithesis of Irish republicanism.
OL,15,F"These bonfires disgracefully imitate
OL,16,Fthe most offensive aspects of loyalist
OL,17,Fbonfires in their sectarianism, their
OL,18,Fcriminality and recklessness.
OL,26,@kD@GrrnD@brrpD@aOUwD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G7/10
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,413,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41208
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F412A1786915122
OL,3,CSinn Fein condemn burning of images of
OL,4,CFirst Minister on bonfire
OL,6,F"The small number of young people and
OL,7,Fchildren involved, often manipulated
OL,8,Fby others who stand in the shadows,
OL,9,Fare not representative of the majority
OL,10,Fof young people who are engaged in
OL,11,Fpositive and productive cultural
OL,12,Factivities all year round."
OL,14,FThe MP added: "At the Fleadh and Feile
OL,15,Fin Belfast and in the Derry Feile we
OL,16,Fsee the future of this island in the
OL,17,Fpositive and inclusive celebration of
OL,18,FIrish culture and identity.
OL,26,@kD@GrrnD@AOUtD@[O]vD@OOUvD@crrwD@^rr
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G8/10
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,413,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41209
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F412A1786915122
OL,3,CSinn Fein condemn burning of images of
OL,4,CFirst Minister on bonfire
OL,6,F"The isolated events in Derry last
OL,7,Fnight are the opposite and can have no
OL,8,Fpart in that future."
OL,10,FRepublican and loyalist bonfires
OL,11,Fcontinue to be a source of controversy
OL,12,Fin Northern Ireland.
OL,14,FBonfire builders from both communities
OL,15,Fhave provoked anger in the past by
OL,16,Fburning symbols associated with the
OL,17,Fother side's culture.
OL,26,@kD@GrrnD@AOUpD@UO]
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G9/10
